# P3.3: Attack Escalation Pattern
# Detects devices that transition from normal to malicious behavior
#
# Formal Specification (MFOTL):
#   escalation_pattern(d, t) ←
#     ◇[10,60] safe_tx(d) ∧
#     ◇[0,50] overflow(d) ∧
#     ◇[0,50] time_anomaly(d)
#
# Equivalent (Mathematical Logic):
#   ∃t₁, t₂, t₃.
#     (t-60 ≤ t₁ ≤ t-10) ∧    # safe_tx was 10-60s ago
#     (t-50 ≤ t₂ ≤ t) ∧       # overflow in last 50s
#     (t-50 ≤ t₃ ≤ t) ∧       # time_anomaly in last 50s
#     safe_tx(d, t₁) ∧ overflow(d, t₂) ∧ time_anomaly(d, t₃)
#
# Semantics: Device was normal (safe_tx 10-60s ago) AND now shows
#            concurrent attacks (overflow + time_anomaly) → escalation

# MonPoly formula (direct MFOTL with free variable d)
# Device was safe 10-60s ago AND now shows concurrent attacks
# Free variable d will appear in output: @ts. (...): (device_name)
(ONCE[10,60] safe_tx(d, _)) AND
(ONCE[0,50] overflow(d, _)) AND
(ONCE[0,50] time_anomaly(d, _))